# ImprintID environment configuration — for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT only.
# On Vercel, these are set in the dashboard instead (Project Settings →
# Environment Variables), not in a file.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE LOCALLY:
# 1. Copy this file and rename the copy to exactly:  .env
# 2. Fill in the values below.
# 3. Run `npm start` (or restart it if already running).

# --- Database (required) ---------------------------------------------------
# After creating a Postgres database in your Vercel project (Storage tab →
# Create Database → Postgres), open its ".env.local" tab — Vercel shows you
# a POSTGRES_URL value there. Copy that exact value here so your local
# server talks to the same database Vercel uses in production.
POSTGRES_URL=

# --- Business Central (optional) -------------------------------------------
# See business-central-api-request.md for what to ask your IT team/BC
# partner for. Leave blank to leave that integration off — everything else
# works fine without it.
BC_TENANT_ID=
BC_CLIENT_ID=
BC_CLIENT_SECRET=
BC_ENVIRONMENT=Production
BC_COMPANY_ID=
BC_COMPANY_NAME=
